---
import PrimerChat from "../PrimerChat.astro";
import { aiCardId, aiTurn, archiveAi } from "../../../lib/archive-ai";

const card = archiveAi["carry-it"];
const kg = { whole: 12, fraction: 12.8 };
const axis = { lo: kg.whole - 1, hi: kg.whole + 2 };
const at = (x: number) => `${((x - axis.lo) / (axis.hi - axis.lo)) * 100}%`;
const ticks = Array.from({ length: axis.hi - axis.lo + 1 }, (_, i) => axis.lo + i);
const shipments = [kg.whole, kg.fraction];

const revised = 12.4;
const kgs = (x: number) => `${x} kg`;
const bound = (x: number) => `${Math.floor(x)} to under ${Math.floor(x) + 1} kg`;
type Fate = "exact" | "bound" | "row" | "file";
const worlds: { id: string; tab: string; kept: string; recover: string; needed: string; claim: [string, string]; fates: [Fate, Fate] }[] = [
  {
    id: "every",
    tab: "Every version",
    kept: "Every raw submission, with its import history",
    recover: `It can replay the submissions in order and rebuild the exact weights suppliers reported at each point in time. If a supplier first sent ${kgs(kg.fraction)} and later revised it to ${kgs(revised)}, both versions are recoverable.`,
    needed: "It already has the essentials for this bug. The original files preserve the weights, and the import history shows which version was used when.",
    claim: ["Exact", "is-ok"],
    fates: ["exact", "exact"],
  },
  {
    id: "table",
    tab: "Processed table only",
    kept: "Only the processed table",
    recover: `It can flag rows imported during the affected period. A stored ${kgs(kg.whole)} means the supplier reported at least ${kgs(kg.whole)} and less than ${kgs(kg.whole + 1)}. The row may already be correct if the supplier reported exactly ${kgs(kg.whole)}. The roaster can calculate bounds for totals, but any single estimate requires assumptions about the missing fractions. The exact reported weights are lost from this archive.`,
    needed: "It needed the original reported weights linked to the processed rows. To recover earlier versions too, it needed to retain each version and its import time.",
    claim: ["Bounded", "is-bad"],
    fates: ["row", "bound"],
  },
  {
    id: "over",
    tab: "Overwritten on resubmission",
    kept: "Raw files, with each resubmission overwriting that supplier's previous file",
    recover: `It can recover exact weights as reported in the surviving files. If the surviving file says ${kgs(revised)}, that establishes the revised weight. The earlier weight could have been ${kgs(kg.fraction)}, but the surviving file cannot establish it. Where an older processed row survives, the roaster can still flag it and give the same rounding bounds.`,
    needed: "It needed to keep each resubmission as a separate version and record which file version each import used.",
    claim: ["Partly exact", "is-warn"],
    fates: ["file", "exact"],
  },
];
const versions = [
  { name: "First submission", weight: kg.fraction },
  { name: "Resubmission", weight: revised },
];
const fateText = (f: Fate, w: number): [string, string] =>
  f === "exact" ? [`${kgs(w)}, from its file`, "is-ok"]
  : f === "bound" ? [`${bound(w)}, from its rounded row`, "is-warn"]
  : f === "row" ? ["Unavailable: its row now holds the resubmission", "is-bad"]
  : ["Unavailable: its file was overwritten, its row updated", "is-bad"];

const checks = [
  ["Weather monitoring", "A station's importer rounded rainfall readings down to whole millimeters. It kept every raw upload and a log of when each version was used. What can it reconstruct about last spring's readings, including later revisions?"],
  ["Payroll", "An importer rounded hours down to whole hours. Only the processed table survives, and one row shows 7 hours. What can you say about the original entry, and what would you need to calculate the exact pay correction?"],
  ["Library inventory", "An importer rounded replacement costs down to whole dollars. Each branch's latest upload overwrote its previous file. A surviving file lists a book at $18.75, and an older processed row shows $18. What would you say in a correction note about those two records?"],
];
---

<PrimerChat
  prompt={card.prompt}
  module="Module 2"
  back={`../02-archive/#${aiCardId("carry-it")}`}
  about="This is a reply an AI assistant gave to Module 2's transfer study prompt, lightly edited. Send the same prompt yourself and you will get a different reply."
  turn={aiTurn("carry-it", "Part 9")}
>
  <h2 class="pr-title">One bug, three archives</h2>
  <p>For six months, a coffee roaster's importer rounded every shipment weight <strong>down</strong> to a whole kilogram. A supplier's <code>{kgs(kg.fraction)}</code> became <code>{kgs(kg.whole)}</code>. The roaster fixes the importer so it preserves the reported weight.</p>
  <p class="pr-pull">What it can correct for those six months depends on what it kept.</p>
  <h2>1. What each archive can recover</h2>
  <p>Assume the processed table has one row per shipment, with a shipment ID and an import date. Suppliers sometimes resubmitted files with revised weights.</p>
  <figure class="pr-card">
    <p class="pr-label">Two weights, one stored value</p>
    <div class="pa-merge">
      <div class="pa-merge-in"><p><code>{kg.whole.toFixed(1)} kg</code></p><p><code>{kg.fraction} kg</code></p></div>
      <p class="pr-arrow"><span>importer</span></p>
      <div class="pa-merge-out"><p><code>{kg.whole} kg</code><span>at least {kg.whole}, less than {kg.whole + 1}</span></p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pa-line" role="img" aria-label={`Number line: a stored ${kg.whole} kg covers every weight from ${kg.whole} up to but not including ${kg.whole + 1} kg. Both shipments, ${kg.whole.toFixed(1)} and ${kg.fraction} kg, fall inside it.`}>
      <div class="pa-line-track">
        <span class="pa-line-band" style={`left:${at(kg.whole)};width:calc(${at(kg.whole + 1)} - ${at(kg.whole)})`}></span>
        {shipments.map((x) => <span class="pa-line-dot" style={`left:${at(x)}`}><small>{x.toFixed(1)}</small></span>)}
      </div>
      <div class="pa-line-ticks" aria-hidden="true">{ticks.map((t) => <span style={`left:${at(t)}`}>{t} kg</span>)}</div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>The stored value fixes a range, not a weight: the shaded kilogram. That range is all a processed table can offer.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure class="pr-card pa-worlds">
    <p class="pr-label">One shipment, revised once: what each archive can give back</p>
    <fieldset class="pr-seg">
      <legend>What the roaster kept</legend>
      {worlds.map((w, i) => <label><input type="radio" name="pa-carry-world" value={w.id} checked={i === 0} /><span>{w.tab}</span></label>)}
    </fieldset>
    <div aria-live="polite">
    {worlds.map((w) => (
      <div class="pa-world" data-world={w.id}>
        <p class="pa-world-head"><span class="pa-world-kept">{w.kept}</span><span class:list={["pr-chip", w.claim[1]]}>{w.claim[0]}</span></p>
        <ul class="pa-versions">{versions.map((v, i) => {
          const [text, tone] = fateText(w.fates[i], v.weight);
          return <li><span>{v.name}</span><span class:list={["pr-chip", tone]}>{text}</span></li>;
        })}</ul>
        <p class="pr-label">What it can honestly recover</p>
        <p>{w.recover}</p>
        <p class="pr-label">What it needed to keep for full recovery</p>
        <p>{w.needed}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
    </div>
    <figcaption>This figure follows one resubmitted shipment: with one row per shipment, its row is replaced too, so no older rounded row is left. The reply's bounds cover shipments whose files are gone but whose rows remain.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>2. What to put in a correction note</h2>
  <p>A correction note should name the evidence behind the correction. For the archive that overwrote older files, the roaster could write:</p>
  <blockquote class="pa-note">
    <p>From January through June, the importer rounded shipment weights down to whole kilograms. We restored the reported precision for shipment records we could match to retained supplier files. When a supplier resubmitted a file, the archive replaced the previous version. For earlier records where only the rounded value survives, we can give a range, but the exact weight originally reported is unavailable from our archive.</p>
  </blockquote>
  <aside class="pr-course" aria-label="Course note">
    <p class="pr-label">Course note</p>
    <p>The reply's three archives are Part 9's three worlds, moved from a clinic network to a coffee roaster. Every raw submission is World A, only the processed table is World B, and overwritten on resubmission is World C.</p>
    <p>The reply's overwrite case draws the line World C's claims must respect: exact for what a surviving file holds, bounded where only a rounded row survives. The latest file is not evidence of what an earlier one held. Each stored weight gives the roaster a range one kilogram wide. A clinic table that filed follow-up visits as new patients gives a range on a count instead: of the rows marked new patient that no surviving form can check, anywhere from none to all might have been follow-ups.</p>
  </aside>

  <h2>3. Check your understanding</h2>
  <ol class="pr-checks">{checks.map(([field, q]) => <li><b>{field}</b><span>{q}</span></li>)}</ol>
</PrimerChat>

<style>
  .pa-worlds .pr-seg { margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .pa-world { display: none; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--tl-line); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--tl-bg); }
  .pa-worlds:has([value="every"]:checked) [data-world="every"],
  .pa-worlds:has([value="table"]:checked) [data-world="table"],
  .pa-worlds:has([value="over"]:checked) [data-world="over"] { display: block; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-worlds p { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-worlds p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-worlds .pr-label { margin: 0 0 0.15rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-world-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem 0.6rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem !important; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-world-kept { color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 700; }
  .pa-merge { display: grid; gap: 0.4rem; align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 46rem) { .pa-merge { grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; } }
  .pa-merge-in, .pa-merge-out { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-merge-in p, :global(.pr) .pa-merge-out p { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0; padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem; border: 1px solid var(--tl-line); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--tl-bg); font-size: 0.88rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-merge-out p { border: 1.5px dashed var(--pr-red); }
  .pa-merge-out span { color: var(--tl-muted); }
  .pa-line { margin: 2.1rem 0.8rem 0.4rem; }
  .pa-line-track { position: relative; height: 0.5rem; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--tl-line); }
  .pa-line-band { position: absolute; top: -0.35rem; bottom: -0.35rem; border: 1.5px dashed var(--pr-red); border-right-style: none; border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pr-red) 18%, transparent); }
  .pa-line-dot { position: absolute; top: 50%; width: 0.8rem; height: 0.8rem; margin: -0.4rem 0 0 -0.4rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--sl-color-white); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--tl-bg); }
  .pa-line-dot small { position: absolute; bottom: 0.95rem; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); color: var(--sl-color-white); font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .pa-line-ticks { position: relative; height: 1.4rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .pa-line-ticks span { position: absolute; transform: translateX(-50%); color: var(--tl-muted); font-size: 0.78rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  :global(.pr-thread) { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .pa-worlds :global(.pr-chip) { white-space: normal; }
  .pa-versions { display: grid; gap: 0.3rem; margin: 0 0 0.7rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .pa-versions li { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 0.3rem 0.6rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.55rem; border: 1px solid var(--tl-line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .pa-note { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding: 0.7rem 0.95rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--pr-yellow); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--tl-card); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-note p { margin: 0; }
</style>
